static block:
“Static blocks are used for automatic execution when a class loads.
Interfaces are meant to be a blueprint or contract — they don’t get loaded to execute code like classes do.
That’s why automatic execution via static blocks is not allowed in interfaces.
However, static methods are allowed, but they only run when explicitly called, not automatically.””



5.inside tthe interface main method is not allowed,since java8 allowed
=>Why it IS allowed (very simple)
  main() is static
  Interface allows static methods (Java 8+)
-Interface cannot create objects, but
-main() does not need an object to run.
✅ Allowed in interface (with Java version)
______________________________________________________
| Feature                               | Notes                                                             | Since Java Version               |
| ------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------- |
| **Abstract methods**                  | Must be implemented by classes                                    | Java 1.0+                        |
| **Constants (`public static final`)** | Variables inside interface are always constants                   | Java 1.0+                        |
| **Static methods**                    | Can have method with body, called explicitly using interface name | Java 8+                          |
| **Default methods**                   | Can have method with body, inherited by implementing class        | Java 8+                          |
| **Main method**                       | Static main method is allowed                                     | Java 8+ (because main is static) |

❌ Not allowed in interface
| Feature                | Reason                                                             | Java Version |
| ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------ |
| **Instance variables** | Interface cannot have objects → only constants allowed             | All versions |
| **Constructor**        | Interface cannot create objects → constructor meaningless          | All versions |
| **Instance blocks**    | Run when object is created → interface has no objects              | All versions |
| **Static blocks**      | Run automatically when class loads → interface is just a blueprint | All versions |

