-the marker interface does not cointain any methods but whenever our class implements that interface
our class aquire some capabilities to perform some operations, such type of interfaces are called as marker interfaces

- marker interface is empty interface, but class is aquiring capabilities these capabilities are provided by JVM

- the process of creating exactly duplicat object is called cloning process

- to make the cloning process the class must implement Clonable interface
to create the cloning use clone() method and this method present in Object class.
-throws java.lang.CloneNotSupportedException;
clone() method throws This exception.
it is checked exception so handle the exception using try-catch or throws keyword.

note:user defined empty interfaces are not a marker interfaces
interface It1{
}


-A marker interface is an interface with NO methods.
-👉 To give information (mark) to JVM or Java classes.
🔹 Famous Marker Interfaces in Java
| Interface      | Purpose                          |
| -------------- | -------------------------------- |
| `Serializable` | Allow object to be saved to file |
| `Cloneable`    | Allow object cloning             |
| `RandomAccess` | Fast access in List              |

Cloning process:
👉 Cloning means creating an exact copy of an object.
Step-by-step:

Class implements Cloneable (marker interface)
Override clone() method
Call super.clone()
JVM creates field-by-field copy

*“Marker interfaces are used to inform JVM about special behavior.
 Cloneable is a marker interface that allows object cloning using the clone() method.”

